  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 105 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nMonday an upper trough along the west coast will begin to move\ninland and turn the flow over TX to the southwest. With moisture\nin the vertical increasing, we will begin to see showers develop\nduring the afternoon. This pattern will repeat each day through\nWednesday. Chances for rain will be confined to the Coastal Plains\nand I-35 Corridor. In addition to the rain chances, temperatures\nwill increase into the middle of the week. With the higher\nhumidity heat indices will push back above 100 degrees for most of\nthe CWA. Models continue to move the upper trough across the \ncentral Rockies and into the Plains bringing a cold front. \nHowever, today they are a bit drier, and we have lower POPs and \nQPF for the latter part of the week. Despite the lower rain \nchances, temperatures are lower behind the front for Friday and \nSaturday.",
